# fullcell_physical: Li-S full cell with PHYSICALLY BASED kinetics on both
# electrodes (docs/KINETICS_TABLE.md): Butler-Volmer plating/stripping from the
# measured j0, CE-anchored electrolyte reduction, cathode cascade with the
# standard potentials of Kumaresan 2008 and exchange rates of Marinescu 2016,
# shuttle from Mikhaylik 2004. Thin cathode (N/P ~ 0.7). Half-cycle = 800 events.
seed 8597
temperature 298
saltMolar 1.2
solvMolar 6.5
scanIntervalType time
potentialType step
scanInterval 3600
maxInterval 800
BeginV 4.4
EndV 2.8
totalSteps 100000
maxCycles 200
printStepFreq 1
XYZprintFreq 500
snapshotEveryCycles 20
checkpointEveryCycles 20
globalA 0.5
numberDecompositionRxns 25
nMobilityReactions 3
# ---- Li-S coupling (new) ---------------------------------------------------
li_pool_mode shared
li_pool_init -1
reservoir_sites 2000
# anode bulk foil: 0 = NO hidden Li reservoir. The anode Li inventory is the
# lattice slab only (conservative anode: stripping thins it, plating rebuilds
# it). With -1 (legacy semi-infinite foil) the framework refilled every
# stripped vacancy and the slab inflated by the plated amount every cycle,
# drying the electrolyte in ~10 cycles (smoke test 2026-09-23). N/P is set by
# the slab thickness in GEOMETRY.in.
li_bulk_init 0
# ---- structural brakes (2026-09-21) ----------------------------------------
# li_pool_max: 2 * li_pool0 (74 Li+ in this box) -> mean-field current
# coupling of the two electrodes (no stripping / cathodic oxidation when the
# electrolyte cannot take more Li+). stop_electrolyte_fraction: clean stop
# when ETH+SOL+FSI fall below 5 % of the initial count (cell dried out).
li_pool_max 148
stop_electrolyte_fraction 0.05
stop_anode_inactive_halves 6
# ---- physically based anode kinetics (see cases/anode_physical) -------------
anode_kinetics bv
bv_k0_site 74
bv_alpha 0.5
eta_charge -0.03
eta_discharge 0.03
# ---- physically based cathode kinetics ------------------------------------
# REGION cathode rates evaluated at the cathode potential of the half-cycle:
# charge plateau 2.45 V, discharge cut-off region 1.9 V (vs Li/Li+); typical
# Li-S plateaus (Kumaresan 2008 Fig. 1; Marinescu 2016 Fig. 2). Tag [P] for
# the exact values, to be replaced by the cell voltage of the reference data.
cathode_kinetics bv
cathode_V_charge 2.45
cathode_V_discharge 1.9
# ---- cycling protocol -------------------------------------------------------
# The cell is assembled charged (Li anode + S8 cathode): the first half-cycle
# is a discharge. A half-cycle also ends after 50 consecutive events without
# Li transfer (zero-current cut-off), so the event budget is not spent on
# electrolyte decomposition once the cathode is fully converted.
first_half end
end_half_when_idle 50
